From eb20edda4a47925064651110a879559a94099b74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:01:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libvpl: Revert va_drm.h include path to this fork's nested
 libva layout

A real flashfiles build failed with a fatal file-not-found error:
hello-encode's util.hpp includes "va/va_drm.h", which the v2.16.0
upgrade (59a14e7) changed from "va//drm/va_drm.h" -- assuming vanilla
upstream libva's flat <includedir>/va/va_drm.h install layout.

This fork's libva (hardware/intel/external/libva) keeps va_drm.h at
its original source-tree path, va/drm/va_drm.h (confirmed unchanged by
the earlier libva 2.23.0 overlay too, and already fixed the same way
in vpl-gpu-rt's libmfxsw.cpp/libmfx_core_vaapi.cpp). No -I flag in any
of these examples' builds resolves the "va/"-prefixed form.

Reverted the identical include across all 11 affected example
sources (legacy-decode/encode/vpp, hello-decode/decvpp/encode/
encode-jpeg/transcode/vpp, hello-sharing-vaapi, vpl-infer) back to
"va/drm/va_drm.h". hello-sharing-vaapi's device-vaapi.h also
includes "va/va_drmcommon.h", which is unaffected -- that header is
genuinely flat in this fork's libva layout (va/va_drmcommon.h) and
needed no change.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
